{"id":"73dc577c58df","html":"<div><div><div><p>You are here: <span><a href=\"https://austinkleon.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><span>Blog</span></a></span> <span aria-label=\"breadcrumb separator\">/</span> <span><a href=\"https://austinkleon.com/category/newspaper-blackout-poems/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><span>Newspaper Blackout Poems</span></a></span> <span aria-label=\"breadcrumb separator\">/</span> On nemeses</p></div>\n<p><time datetime=\"2026-10-26T15:50:49-04:00\">Monday, October 26, 2026</time>  </p><div><p><img src=\"https://austinkleon.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/image-2-600x793.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"600\" height=\"793\" sizes=\"(max-width: 600px) 100vw, 600px\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>I used this poem at the top of my letter, “<a href=\"https://austinkleon.substack.com/p/everything-you-can-see\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Everything you can see</a>.”</p>\n<p>See also: “<a href=\"https://austinkleon.substack.com/p/do-you-have-a-nemesis\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Do you have a nemesis?</a>”</p>\n</div></div></div>"}